# Testing

Tests should validate behavior and invariants rather than implementation details.

Behavioral changes involving any of the following require appropriate tests:
- concurrency
- cancellation
- timeouts
- retries
- queue/backpressure behavior
- trajectory schemas
- serialization
- worker lifecycle
- error handling
- policy/model versioning

## Async

Test:
- successful completion
- cancellation
- timeout
- producer failure
- consumer failure
- shutdown while work is active
- bounded queue behavior

Avoid arbitrary sleep-based synchronization.

## Go concurrency

Run:

    go test -race ./...

for concurrency-sensitive changes.

## Regression tests

A production bug should normally result in a regression test that would fail before the fix.

## Verification

Do not claim tests passed unless they were actually run.
If a required check cannot run, report the reason explicitly.
